dist/
.vite/
*.local

# Working material, not project documentation. The predecessor-project audits, the scaffold
# sequencing and its review are inputs to the first few commits, not a record of this project.
# The durable decisions in them get promoted into the constitution and docs/decisions/, which
# are NOT ignored — only these three paths are, so a real doc tree can land beside them.
#
# They are deliberately kept on disk rather than deleted: the plan and its review are the
# snapshot of how this repo was intended to start, and the point of comparison for how it
# actually went. Neither is maintained after the scaffold lands — going stale is the intent.
docs/extraction/
docs/scaffold-plan.md
docs/plan-review-2026-08-03.md

# Milestone records — written as each milestone lands, so the next project starts faster than this
# one did. Ignored for the same reason as the three above: they are about HOW this repo was built,
# not about what it is, and a future contributor cloning it needs the decisions rather than the
# retrospectives.
#
# ⚠️ NAMED COST, since it is a real one: gitignored means machine-local. These survive neither a
# fresh machine nor a clone, and the whole point of them is to be read by the NEXT project. They are
# reached the way CLAUDE.md reaches the predecessor — by absolute path. If a machine change is ever
# on the cards, copy the folder first; nothing else will.
docs/milestones/

# Facts about THIS computer — the toolchain's location, and the map of configuration that lives
# outside git. Ignored because a clone on another machine needs none of it and would be misled by
# all of it. It was previously inside docs/scaffold-plan.md, which is explicitly not maintained past
# RELEASE, so the only record of how to run node sat in a file scheduled to be deleted.
docs/machine.md
